{"schema_version":"1.7.5","id":"JLSEC-2026-1007","published":"2026-07-30T16:02:27.435Z","modified":"2026-07-30T18:35:35.495097502Z","upstream":["CVE-2026-45031","EUVD-2026-36157","GHSA-cwpj-h54c-xjpx"],"summary":"ImageMagick: Policy Bypass in PSD decoder","details":"ImageMagick is free and open-source software used for editing and manipulating digital images. Prior to versions 6.9.13-47 and 7.1.2-22, due to a missing check in the PSD decoder it would be possible to bypass the list-length resource policy when decoding a PSD image. Other security limits would still apply. This issue has been patched in versions 6.9.13-47 and 7.1.2-22.","affected":[{"package":{"name":"ImageMagick_jll","ecosystem":"Julia","purl":"pkg:julia/ImageMagick_jll?uuid=c73af94c-d91f-53ed-93a7-00f77d67a9d7"},"ranges":[{"type":"SEMVER","events":[{"introduced":"0"},{"fixed":"7.1.2028+0"}]}],"database_specific":{"source":"https://github.com/JuliaLang/SecurityAdvisories.jl/tree/generated/osv/2026/JLSEC-2026-1007.json"}}],"references":[{"type":"WEB","url":"https://access.redhat.com/errata/RHSA-2026:32961"},{"type":"WEB","url":"https://access.redhat.com/security/cve/CVE-2026-45031"},{"type":"WEB","url":"https://bugzilla.redhat.com/show_bug.cgi?id=2487734"},{"type":"WEB","url":"https://github.com/ImageMagick/ImageMagick/security/advisories/GHSA-cwpj-h54c-xjpx"},{"type":"WEB","url":"https://github.com/advisories/GHSA-cwpj-h54c-xjpx"},{"type":"WEB","url":"https://nvd.nist.gov/vuln/detail/CVE-2026-45031"},{"type":"WEB","url":"https://security.access.redhat.com/data/csaf/v2/vex/2026/cve-2026-45031.json"}],"database_specific":{"license":"CC-BY-4.0","sources":[{"database_specific":{"status":"Modified"},"html_url":"https://nvd.nist.gov/vuln/detail/CVE-2026-45031","id":"CVE-2026-45031","imported":"2026-07-30T14:08:47.026Z","modified":"2026-07-23T09:10:00.113Z","published":"2026-06-10T22:16:57.800Z","url":"https://services.nvd.nist.gov/rest/json/cves/2.0?cveId=CVE-2026-45031"},{"html_url":"https://github.com/adv